{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED. Independent review of the bounded whole-projection implementation at exact head aa86e7dd375dd93a437f12f59e0ab314b281c16d, reviewed in a clean detached worktree at that commit. The head is one commit on top of main 5fc9929c, its merge-base, and carries Rests-On the governing request a7752131. All eleven changed files were read in full.\n\nBOUNDING. Totals are exact and computed before any cap: actorTotals walks the whole projection (every commitment, every artifact, every decision, len(Statements)) and never sees a capped slice. Measured against a clone of the live log at depth 6174, every field of the bounded response equals the unbounded projection: depth 6174, statements 4166, artifacts 1149, stale artifacts 1091, ineffective 87, disputed 1, and the identical commitments-by-status map. Caps report honestly: not_actionable carried 20 rows with not_actionable_skipped 613. Row selection is Cap keeping the most recent ListCap=20 in fold order, and actorAttention re-derives its order from projection.Decisions, so selection is deterministic. Sizes: POST /v0/actor-status 43,807 bytes against GET /v0/status 11,931,501 and POST /v0/status 11,931,523; POST /v0/actor-wait 21,280 bytes against POST /v0/wait 11,931,547. That is 272x on status and 560x on the poll path agents hit continuously. The 500,000-record benchmark reproduces at 575 response bytes, 0.87 ms/op, 1,556 B/op.\n\nThe 1 MiB ceiling is enforced in residentclient.read by reading limit+1 bytes and refusing above the limit, so the boundary is a clean explicit error rather than truncation or a partial decode; the error is not a transport error, so it surfaces to the caller instead of silently falling back. Wait semantics are preserved exactly: handleWait and handleActorWait share one s.wait helper with the identical Poll predicate, so the wake-on-change contract is unchanged and only the encoding differs, with the long-poll deadline extended to the new path.\n\nCOMPATIBILITY. The change is additive. GET and POST /v0/status and POST /v0/wait still serve the complete projection; durable.projection still parses, so existing board and cron consumers are unaffected. No file under cmd/gs changed, so gs status --json and --all are untouched. Version skew is forgiving both ways: an old adapter keeps using the old routes, and a new adapter against an old resident gets 404, which inboxProtocolUnavailable already routes to the local degraded fallback. The degraded fallback still passes degraded=true on both tools.\n\nARCHITECTURE. Affected layers are 3 Nexus and live runtime, 6 Projections and queries, and 7 CLI, MCP, skills, connectors and UI. All three contracts are preserved and no contract changed, so docs/reference/architecture.md correctly needed no edit in this head; it enumerates no routes. Layer 3: Observe returns the actor and full fingerprint the lease already held, captured under the same lock as the private inbox, and both fields are json:\"-\" so they never cross the nexus wire boundary; the nexus still handles opaque fingerprints. Layer 6: that layer is already defined as the place bounded queries select from derived state, so moving status and wait selection into internal/statusview honors the layer rather than changing it. Layer 7: internal/service gains two routes within its composing role, and the MCP surface contract is unchanged by construction because actorStatus and waitDelta are type aliases of the statusview types, so the resident path and the local fallback cannot drift in shape. The application-host and profile boundary is untouched.\n\nSECURITY. No new authority. Both routes are read-only and take session as their only identity input; decode uses DisallowUnknownFields behind a 2 MiB MaxBytesReader, so an actor or fingerprint field in the body is refused with HTTP 400, which I confirmed against a running resident. Identity and the private inbox come from one Observe under one nexus lock after expiry, so there is no split between who you are and whose inbox you get, and no expiry or rebind race. Rebinding a live session to another actor is refused. A missing session and an unknown session both fail closed with 400; anonymous callers cannot reach these routes. An empty fingerprint is unreachable over HTTP because handleAnnounce resolves the actor through workspace.Actor before binding the lease. A session announced as another actor does see that actor's view, but that is pre-existing presence behaviour on a loopback-only single-operator host per 8a758fb7, and these routes narrow identity from a request parameter to the session rather than widening it. No secret or key material appears in either response. The race gate is clean on service, nexus and statusview.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION. The change is net subtractive where it matters: it deletes two whole-log index maps from the hot paths and replaces them with one bounded scan each. I found nothing to cut that would not weaken boundedness, identity binding, compatibility or fallback, so no changes are requested. Four non-blocking observations for later work: fillCommitmentText could key map[string]*CommitmentView since each commitment lands in exactly one lane per build; handleActorStatus repeats the session/Observe/statusFromLive preamble of handleSessionStatus and could share a helper the way the two wait handlers now do; actorAttention still materializes an actor's non-effective events before capping, which is bounded in practice and strictly better than before but is the one lane whose pre-cap working set still grows with history; and query.go still builds whole-log statementIndex and actIndex for work and inspect, which is the same defect one layer over and deserves its own request.\n\nMUTATION SPOT-CHECKS. Four mutations, four caught, tree restored clean afterwards. Counting totals after the cap turned TestStatusDigestIsActorOrientedAndBounded red with \"totals do not describe the whole projection\". Changing actorStatusResponseLimit from 1 MiB turned TestStatusAndWaitUseBoundedResidentViews red. Pointing status back at /v0/status turned the same test red on its blocked-route assertion. Removing the post-cap fillCommitmentText call turned TestActorStatusAndWaitExposeOpenAddressedWorkWithoutInventingAPromise red on the lost request label.\n\nGATES at the exact clean head: go build ./... clean, go vet ./... clean, go test ./... -count=1 exit 0 across 25 packages including the internal/docset documentation gates, and go test -race on internal/service, internal/nexus and internal/statusview clean.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:176adca6ab73ff05662dc6e2efa8cdb1e607f98e","head":"aa86e7dd375dd93a437f12f59e0ab314b281c16d","verdict":"approved"}}